# UX workflow: verify chord strum preview uses step-relative timing.
# Purpose: Strum 0 should show simultaneous voices; increasing Strum should
# spread voice markers across the step proportionally to the edited value.
# Expect: capture_changed:strum_zero=strum_adjusted, capture_changed:velocity_curve_zero=velocity_curve_adjusted

0 scenario sequencer
50 capture screen sequencer_ready

# Move to Step focus, enable step 1, and open the Step Editor.
150 tap NAV 60
350 capture screen pattern_focus
450 tap NAV 60
650 capture screen step_focus
750 tap MACRO_1 60
950 capture screen step_1_enabled
1050 button MACRO_1 down
2100 tick
2150 capture screen step_editor_open
2200 button MACRO_1 up

# Focus Chord, create a local chord, and open Chord detail.
2300 encoder NAV 1
2380 encoder NAV 1
2460 encoder NAV 1
2540 encoder NAV 1
2620 encoder NAV 1
2700 encoder NAV 1
2850 encoder OPT 1.0
3050 tap NAV 60

# Move to Strum field: Mode -> Voices -> Color -> Shape -> Spread -> Strum.
3150 encoder NAV 1
3230 encoder NAV 1
3310 encoder NAV 1
3390 encoder NAV 1
3470 encoder NAV 1
3650 capture screen strum_zero
3750 encoder OPT 1.0
3950 capture screen strum_adjusted

# Move to Velocity curve and verify it has distinct top-title feedback while
# the chord map remains readable.
4050 encoder NAV 1
4250 capture screen velocity_curve_zero
4350 encoder OPT 1.0
4550 capture screen velocity_curve_adjusted
